### What is cohesion and why is high cohesion a design goal?

Cohesion is about focus within a single class. High cohesion means every method and field serves one clear purpose.

### What does a God class look like (low cohesion)?

```java
// WRONG: God class does everything (3000+ lines, 50+ methods)
public class BankingManager {
    public Account createAccount(String name) { /* ... */ }
    public void closeAccount(String id) { /* ... */ }
    public Trade executeTrade(String symbol, int qty) { /* ... */ }
    public void cancelTrade(String tradeId) { /* ... */ }
    public void sendSms(String phone, String msg) { /* ... */ }
    public void sendEmail(String email, String msg) { /* ... */ }
    public Report generateDailyReport() { /* ... */ }
    public java.math.BigDecimal calculateBrokerage(java.math.BigDecimal amount) { /* ... */ }
    public boolean checkKYC(String customerId) { /* ... */ }
    // 5 unrelated areas in one class.
    // Changing fee logic might accidentally break notifications.
}
```

### What does high cohesion look like?

```java
// CORRECT: each class does one thing well
public class AccountService {
    public Account createAccount(String name) { /* ... */ }
    public void closeAccount(String id) { /* ... */ }
}

public class TradeExecutionService {
    public Trade executeTrade(String symbol, int qty) { /* ... */ }
    public void cancelTrade(String tradeId) { /* ... */ }
}

public class NotificationService {
    public void sendSms(String phone, String msg) { /* ... */ }
    public void sendEmail(String email, String msg) { /* ... */ }
}

public class FeeCalculator {
    public java.math.BigDecimal calculateBrokerage(java.math.BigDecimal amount) { /* ... */ }
}

public class ComplianceService {
    public boolean checkKYC(String customerId) { /* ... */ }
}
// Each class: 50-200 lines. Easy to understand. Easy to test. Easy to change.
```

### How do you check if a class has high cohesion?

Use the AND test: describe the class in one sentence.

```java
// LOW cohesion:
// "BankingManager creates accounts AND executes trades AND sends notifications AND calculates fees."
// Multiple ANDs = multiple responsibilities.

// HIGH cohesion:
// "FeeCalculator calculates trading fees."
// One sentence, no AND.
```

### What are the benefits of high cohesion?

| Benefit | Low Cohesion (God Class) | High Cohesion |
|---------|------------------------|---------------|
| Understandability | 3000 lines | 50-200 lines |
| Testability | Loads entire system | Tests one thing |
| Changeability | Fee change risks notifications | Fee change is isolated |
| Reusability | Drag entire God class | Use FeeCalculator alone |
| Merge conflicts | Everyone edits same file | Different files |

### What are common mistakes?

The most common mistake is starting with a God class and thinking it is faster because everything is in one place.

### What should a senior engineer know?

- The Single Responsibility Principle (SRP) formalizes high cohesion: a class should have only one reason to change.
- In microservices, high cohesion maps to bounded contexts: each service owns one domain.
- SonarQube measures cohesion metrics like LCOM (Lack of Cohesion of Methods) to detect God classes.
